From b2b5c80e3a14d409bbdc8b4a6dd555e71601ffe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris <boris.potapov@mail.utoronto.ca>
Date: Thu, 30 Oct 2025 22:29:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/30] define environments

we will have a "simulation" environment and "de1-soc" environemnt, and
any other environments we might need down the road; simulation
environment will be used to run testbenches and riscof; de1-soc will be
used to deploy the core + memory (see below) to an FPGA board;

also, here we separate the core from memory; memory was originaly
designed to live "within" the core which is not the case in reality --
core interacts with memory, rather than contains it; we define a
four-line interface here, that will be used both by simulaiton and the
de1-soc; the MA.sv files are different for these two "platforms" because
for the simulation we want to supply an arbitrary mem file while on
de1-soc we will have a preconfigured one;

we will probably need to revice this organization down the road but for
now this might just work
